  "body": "Example: http://output.jsbin.com/damase\nIf the `<body>` underneath a modal `<dialog>` is visible (e.g. due to limiting the dimensions of the `<dialog>`), and the `<body>` is short enough not to need a scrollbar given the current size of the browser window, but the `<dialog>` is tall enough to need a scrollbar, and the user is on a platform with \"classic\" non-auto-hiding scrollbars (e.g. Windows), then opening the modal `<dialog>` will make the viewport narrower due to the requisite scrollbar occupying some width. This in turn causes the `<body>` content to noticeably reflow and \"jump around\". In the example, the red `position:fixed` div shifts to the left (imagine the green bar is a navbar and the red rectangle is a link/button within that navbar), and the `<body>` text is re-line-wrapped (look at the \"A B C D\" paragraph before and afterward).\n\nJudging by the numerous comments on https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/issues/14040, a visually-similar issue affecting Bootstrap's modal dialog widget, it seems that most web designers regard such modal-dialog-related reflow as ugly and undesirable. Since `<dialog>` has so far only been implemented by Blink, perhaps it's still possible to adjust the spec to avoid reflowing in such situations?\n",
